From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] jails/instances/lab-mail: Spec the list's mail hub
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: txyvosqqvyyqkxtsqrrpryxuwskxnsyz
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:53:38 +0000

The list travels as a maildir in jj, pushed and merged like code, so
two sides that both add mail conflict, and agents reach it only
through Pat's merge. lab-mail already holds the Fastmail credentials
and serves mail on loopback, so it can carry the list itself: synced
both ways with Fastmail, posted to over SMTP, and read over IMAP by
every host the same way.

Agents can then add to the list only by posting, and their read-only
logins keep them from changing anything already on it. Nothing leaves
lab-mail except through mbsync into a Fastmail folder, so no relay or
sender allowlist is needed.

Dovecot is the only writer of the maildir, so mbsync and OpenSMTPD
need no access to its files and the per-user permission scheme of the
relay design does not have to stretch to three writers.
