base-branch: b/dev@upstream

This revises the spec in place for the hub design settled in the
thread "[RFC] re-thinking SMTP relay" [1].
It changes only spec.org; the build follows once the spec is agreed.
The spec is identical on trunk and b/dev, so it applies to either.

Decisions taken from the thread:
- OpenSMTPD replaces smtprelay on 127.0.0.1:2525 and never relays.
- Only lab-devel@p7x.dev is delivered; the other known addresses are
  accepted and discarded, and To and Cc are kept.
- Dovecot alone writes the maildir: OpenSMTPD hands mail over LMTP,
  and mbsync syncs Fastmail with Dovecot over IMAP.
- Pat's login is read-write; any other login is read-only.
- Two-way sync of lists and Archive, Expunge None and Remove None.
- Archive by folder, into Fastmail's Archive.
- Mail roots are ~/mail/<login>; Pat imports the jj maildir once; the
  mail bookmark, submissions, and ~/lab/mail.jj are retired.
- The beastie client spec from "[PATCH v2] dotfiles/notmuch: Spec
  reading and sending through lab-mail" [2] is folded in here.

Decisions this spec makes that the thread did not:
- mbsync's Dovecot login has a password of its own, in the secrets
  directory, since every jail on beastie reaches 127.0.0.1:2143.
- The well-formedness check runs in OpenSMTPD's session, so a bad
  message is refused at the end of DATA instead of bouncing to an
  address that is discarded.
- Pat's channel uses Expunge Both and the agent's Expunge Near, so an
  archived message leaves lists on lab-mail and every client.
  Fastmail keeps every message, so a mistaken deletion is recoverable.
- pat@p7x.dev is a known address beside pat@patmaddox.com.

